From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 21:09:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: fsl: rng: fail a read when CAAM rejects the job

run_descriptor_jr() returns a negative value only when the job could
not be queued or dequeued. A job CAAM ran and rejected -- an entropy
test failure in the RNG, say -- comes back as the job's status word,
which is always positive: its source field sits in bits 31:28 and is
never above 7. caam_rng_read_one() tested for ret < 0, so such a job
counted as a success and the caller got priv->data unchanged: zeros
from the allocation on the first read, the previous block after that.

Fail the read on any non-zero return.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 drivers/crypto/fsl/rng.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/crypto/fsl/rng.c b/drivers/crypto/fsl/rng.c
index 06f37a8b4de..9f981339090 100644
--- a/drivers/crypto/fsl/rng.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/fsl/rng.c
@@ -43,8 +43,13 @@ static int caam_rng_read_one(struct caam_rng_priv *priv)
 
 	caam_init_desc(priv);
 
+	/*
+	 * A job CAAM rejects comes back as its positive status word, not as
+	 * a negative errno, and leaves priv->data holding whatever the last
+	 * good job wrote.
+	 */
 	ret = run_descriptor_jr(priv->desc);
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret)
 		return -EIO;
 
 	invalidate_dcache_range((unsigned long)priv->data,
-- 
2.47.3

